      "title": "Data & AI Weekly Ep. 8 | Inside the Streamhouse: A Shared Architecture for the Age of AI | Redpanda",
      "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ylg7FpJ2uPw",
      "published_at": "2026-09-30T23:42:55+00:00",
      "author": "Redpanda Data",
      "summary": "Increasingly enterprises are demanding more than what their lakehouses can provide. Data that's only refreshed through periodic batch processes can't keep pace with applications and AI agents that now do more than analyze what happened in the past — they make decisions and take action as business events unfold, and that requires fresh, governed context delivered continuously, at production service levels. The next evolution is enriching the analytical domain with streaming, real-time data — giving rise to the birth of the streamhouse. Join our panel of speakers as they explore the requirements of a streamhouse architecture, and to learn more about the new Streamhouse Working Group. Redpanda’s Peter Corless will moderate the panel discussion with experts from each of the founding organizations of the working group, including Redpanda’s Matthew Schumpert, StreamNative’s Kundan Vyas and Ververica’s Fabian Wilckens.",
